-- title:
--   Inertia-equivariant crossing chart over A from a chart over O
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ containing the kernel of the reduction $\mathrm{ZMod.unitsMap}$ associated with $M/p \mid M$ (hypothesis `hHp`), with $M/p$ nonzero. Let `hj` record that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by the quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$. Let `𝔛 : XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` be a Deligne–Rapoport model package: it bundles the two-chart integral model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over the ring $R_p$, together with properness, flatness, integrality, local finite presentation and normality of that model, properness and relative smoothness of dimension one at the auxiliary level `ΓN p M H hpM`, a curve model `Meta` of the function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with an isomorphism `eeta` onto the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, compatibility of `eeta` with the arithmetic Galois action, the pinning of the finite chart by $q$-expansion coefficients, and smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre.
--
--   Coefficient data. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ is a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa := \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed, and let $\rho : R_p \to A$ satisfy `hρ`: composing $\rho$ with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ gives the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O : R_p \to O$, whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$ (hypothesis `hϖ`). The comparison data is a ring homomorphism $\iota : O \to A$ subject to: `hι`, that $\iota \circ \rho_O = \rho$; `hιinj`, that $\iota$ is injective; `hιloc`, that $\iota(o)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ if and only if $o$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$; `hιsurj`, that $o \mapsto \mathrm{residue}_A(\iota(o))$ is surjective onto $\kappa$; `hιfix`, that every element $\tau$ of the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ which lies in the inertia subgroup fixes $\iota(o)$ for all $o \in O$; and `htoκ`, that $(\mathrm{residue}_A \circ \iota) \circ \rho_O = \mathrm{residue}_A \circ \rho$.
--
--   The crossing. Write $X_O$ for the scheme `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, the pullback of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` along `Spec.map ρO`, and $X_A$ for the pullback of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` along `Spec.map ρ`; write $X_\kappa$ for `fibre (ΓM M H) hj ((residue A).comp ρ)`. The package supplies two morphisms `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` into $X_\kappa$, which play the role of the two branches through a crossing and in terms of whose images the orientation conditions below are stated. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of these two morphisms. Its image under `pullback.fst` followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and then by `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj ρO ((residue A).comp ι) htoκ` — the canonical morphism $X_\kappa \to X_O$ induced by $\mathrm{residue}_A \circ \iota$ — is denoted $x^O$, and its image under `pullback.fst` followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and then by the morphism `bcA` below is denoted $x^A$. Rationality of the crossing is expressed by a morphism $t : \operatorname{Spec} \kappa \to X_\kappa$ with `ht₁`, that $t$ followed by `pullback.snd` is the identity, and `ht₂`, that $t$ sends the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ to the image of `pullback.fst n` under `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0`.
--
--   The chart over $O$. Let $e \ge 1$, let $U_0$ be an open subscheme of $X_O$ with $x^O \in U_0$ (hypothesis `hxU₀`), and let
--   $$f_0 : U_0 \longrightarrow \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^e)\bigr) = \mathrm{CrossingQuotient.crossingScheme}\,(p^e)$$
--   satisfy: `hover₀`, that $f_0$ followed by the $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $O \to O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-p^e)$ equals the inclusion $U_0 \hookrightarrow X_O$ followed by `pullback.snd`, so that $f_0$ is a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} O$; `hfib₀`, that for a point $y$ of $U_0$ both classes `CrossingQuotient.U` and `CrossingQuotient.V` of the coordinates lie in the prime $f_0(y)$ if and only if $y$ maps to $x^O$; `hpt₀`, that for $y$ mapping to $x^O$ the stalk map of $f_0$ at $y$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal, and induces an isomorphism of residue fields; `het₀`, that for such $y$ there is an open $V \ni y$ in $U_0$ with $V \hookrightarrow U_0$ followed by $f_0$ étale; and the orientation conditions `hor₁`–`hor₄`, that for a point $y$ of $U_0$ the class `V` lies in $f_0(y)$ if and only if the image of $y$ in $X_O$ lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by `bcMap …`, and the class `U` lies in $f_0(y)$ if and only if that image lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` followed by `bcMap …`.
--
--   Finally let `bcA :` $X_\kappa \to X_A$ satisfy `hbcA₁`, that `bcA` followed by `pullback.fst` is `pullback.fst`, and `hbcA₂`, that `bcA` followed by `pullback.snd` equals `pullback.snd` followed by `Spec.map` of $\mathrm{residue}_A$.
--
--   Conclusion. There exist an open subscheme $U$ of $X_A$ with $x^A \in U$ and a morphism
--   $$f : U \longrightarrow \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(A[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^e)\bigr)$$
--   with the same exponent $e$, such that:
--
--   (i) $f$ followed by the $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $A \to A[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-p^e)$ equals the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow X_A$ followed by `pullback.snd`;
--
--   (ii) for every point $y$ of $U$, the classes `U` and `V` of the two coordinates both lie in the prime $f(y)$ if and only if $y$ maps to $x^A$;
--
--   (iii) for every point $y$ of $U$ mapping to $x^A$, the stalk map of $f$ at $y$ is flat, the image ideal of the maximal ideal under it is the maximal ideal, and the induced map on residue fields is an isomorphism;
--
--   (iv) there is an open $W \subseteq U$ containing some point $y$ of $U$ that maps to $x^A$, such that the inclusion $W \hookrightarrow U$ followed by $f$ is étale;
--
--   (v) inertia equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in the inertia subgroup, for all $x', y' \in A$ with $x'y' = p^e$ and such that the images $\tau(x'), \tau(y')$ under the induced ring automorphism of $A$ again satisfy $\tau(x')\tau(y') = p^e$, and for all $s, s' : \operatorname{Spec} A \to U$ which are sections of the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow X_A$ followed by `pullback.snd`, if $s'$ followed by $U \hookrightarrow X_A$ and `pullback.fst` equals `Spec.map` of the automorphism $\tau$ of $A$ followed by $s$, then $U \hookrightarrow X_A$ and `pullback.fst`, and if $s$ followed by $f$ is the $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-algebra map `CrossingQuotient.lift x' y'` sending the two coordinates to $x'$ and $y'$, then $s'$ followed by $f$ is the $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `CrossingQuotient.lift` applied to $\tau(x')$ and $\tau(y')$;
--
--   (vi) for every point $y$ of $U$, if the class `V` lies in $f(y)$ then the image of $y$ in $X_A$ lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by `bcA`;
--
--   (vii) for every point $y$ of $U$, if the class `U` lies in $f(y)$ then the image of $y$ lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` followed by `bcA`;
--
--   (viii) conversely, if the image of $y$ in $X_A$ lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by `bcA` then the class `V` lies in $f(y)$;
--
--   (ix) and if that image lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` followed by `bcA` then the class `U` lies in $f(y)$.
--
--   This is the descent of coefficients step for the local crossing charts on the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ at $p$: a chart $\operatorname{Spec} O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-p^e)$ defined over the discrete valuation ring $O$ with uniformiser $p$ is transported along $\iota : O \to A$ to a chart over the valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, keeping the same exponent, the vertex over the given crossing, flatness and étaleness near the vertex, the orientation by the two branches, and gaining equivariance for the inertia group at $A$ (which fixes $\iota(O)$ pointwise). It is used by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart_valuationSubring`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart_valuationSubring), which provides such charts at every crossing.
